    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: fc4c1c4ceaa9ee3b018dfd2e25098bcf98cfd859 -->\n**Clean code; conflicts with main (mechanical).**\n\n- **Maintainer's 12:57 item:** the seven-file conflict was resolved by the 18:20 merge.\n- **New conflict:** one hunk from later main, in `crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs`, the `pub mod`/`pub use` block. Keep `#[path = \"stock_sim_wire.rs\"] pub mod wire;` and take main's `pub use carry::{...}`/`held::{...}` lines.\n- **Tests (merged tree):** `cargo xtask gate quick` is green: lib plus 32 app binaries, 0 failed, including `wire_readers` 7/7. Clippy is clean.\n- **Sim law:** `simulate_document` refuses a wire cut by name (`stock_sim_wire.rs:32-39`) instead of reading the stock as uncut. The `plan_program` skip is keyed on `!mounts_tool()`, so a milling op with a lost tool is still refused.\n- **Note:** `stock_sim.rs` is 433 lines; it was already over the guideline.\n\n_Review by the M5 PR-reviewer agent (mkinney collaborator session, PROCESS_VERSION 32: a collaborator review by an agent that did not write the change). Trial-merged with upstream main of 2026-11-12 ~21:30Z._\n",
